F_{MIN} = \frac{mg}{\sin\theta^* + \mu_S\cos\theta^*} = \frac{mg}{\frac{1}{\sqrt{1+\mu_S^2}} + \mu_S\frac{\mu_S}{\sqrt{1+\mu_S^2}}} = \frac{mg}{\sqrt{1+\mu_S^2}}.
\] Specularmente, ponendo \(F_A = -\mu_S N\): \[
F\sin\theta = mg + F_A \ge mg + \mu_S N \implies F(\sin\theta - \mu_S\cos\theta) \ge mg \implies F \ge \frac{mg}{\sin\theta^* - \mu_S\cos\theta^*}.
\] Da cui: \[
F_{MAX} = \frac{mg\sqrt{1+\mu_S^2}}{1-\mu_S^2} \implies F_{MAX} = F_{MIN} \frac{1+\mu_S^2}{1-\mu_S^2} \implies F_{MAX} \ge F_{MIN}.
\] Condizione limite se \(F_A \ge 0 \implies F_G = \frac{mg}{\sin\theta^*} = mg\sqrt{1+\mu_S^2}\).


